# Purpose and audience: executable specification evidence for the owning engineering team.
# @req REQ-SSPEC-FEATURE
# research: doc/01_research/domain/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ; plan: doc/03_plan/sspec_modernization_plan.md ; architecture: doc/04_architecture/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md ; design: doc/05_design/infra/sspec/modern_sspec_typed_evidence_design.md

"""
## Purpose and audience

# Minimal Test Spec

**Feature ID:** #TEST-002
**Category:** Infrastructure
**Status:** Active

## Overview

A minimal smoke test that verifies the test runner can load a spec file
with a basic describe/it block and execute a trivial assertion. Used as a
baseline sanity check for the SPipe framework and test infrastructure.

## Syntax

```simple
describe "Test":
it "works":
    # @req REQ-SSPEC-FEATURE
    step("works")
check(true)
```

This specification is maintained for compiler and library engineers reviewing FEATURE-USAGE behavior, and for operators verifying a build.

## Operator workflow

Run `bin/simple test --no-session-daemon test/feature/usage/minimal_spec.spl` and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Each scenario names the requirement it traces to and starts with a Verify step.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers only the behavior explicitly asserted below on the current toolchain. No external standard or cross-version contract is claimed; numeric oracles are explained inline where they appear.

## Recovery and troubleshooting

If a scenario fails, re-run the single spec file, read the first failing Verify step, and compare the reported value against the inline oracle comment before bisecting recent changes.
"""
# @manual: primary
# REQ-FEATURE-USAGE-001
# doc-path: doc/01_research/app/
# doc-path: doc/03_plan/app/
# doc-path: doc/04_architecture/app/
# doc-path: doc/05_design/app/
use db.*
use std.spec.{step}
fn check(condition: bool):
    expect(condition).to_equal(true)
fn check_msg(condition: bool, message: text):
    if not condition:
        expect(message).to_equal("")

describe "Test":
    # @manual scenario evidence
    it "executes a real assertion end to end":
        # @req REQ-SSPEC-FEATURE
        # oracle: the engine's own arithmetic and text ops are the system under test
        expect(6 * 7).to_equal(42)
        expect("smoke".to_upper()).to_equal("SMOKE")
